  "answer": "I'll start by exploring the workspace to find the relevant files.\nNow I'll rename the helper and re-export it under the new name.\nRenamed and verified.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`src/core.ts`** — renamed the exported helper:\n```ts\nexport function sumEntries(values: number[]) { return values.reduce((sum, value) => sum + value, 0) }\n```\n\n**`src/index.ts`** — updated the import, re-exported under the new name, and kept the wrapper's behavior identical:\n```ts\nimport { sumEntries } from './core'\nexport { sumEntries }\nexport const total = (values: number[]) => sumEntries(values)\n```\n\n## Verification\n- A search across `src/` and `test/` returns **no remaining `computeTotal` references**.\n- `bun test` (the existing runner) passes:\n  - `test/oracle.test.ts` → `(pass) sum entries` — **1 pass, 0 fail, 2 expect() calls**\n- `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` were left untouched; no configuration was added and the runner was not replaced.\n\nNote: the test only imports from `src/index.ts`, so the re-export is what makes `sumEntries` resolvable there; `total` still delegates to the same reduce-based implementation it used before."
